  "notes": "Law 20-034/AU of 29 December 2020 makes elementary school five years (ages 6–10) and folds the former first year, CP1, into the last year of pre-elementary (Grande Section); in 2023 some schools still ran CP1 before CP2, so a learner may count one year more. Collège (6e–3e) and lycée (Seconde–Terminale, baccalauréat) follow the French model."
